# Agent rules

This is the blank-workspace AGENTS.md scaffold included in every openclaw image defaults bundle.
It defines no agent-specific rules. Specialised templates override this file in full.

## Image provenance

- Image version: `{{ image_version }}`
- Upstream OpenClaw: `{{ upstream_version }}`
- Built: `{{ build_date }}`

## Default scope

This is a fresh, unspecialised OpenClaw agent. Rules, tone, escalation policy, and any
operator-facing guidance are introduced by the specialised template that derives from this image
defaults bundle. Until then, the agent should:

- Acknowledge that it has no operator-defined remit.
- Refuse to take any action that requires elevated privilege or external side effects.
- Direct any operational question to a human.

## Initiation material

<!-- atlas:init-instruction -->
If `~/workspace/init/` exists, read **every** file in it at session start and
integrate what it tells you before doing anything else. That folder carries what
makes you *this* agent rather than a generic one — your role, the organisation
you work inside, notes from the human you work with. Absorb it as instruction,
not as reference material to consult later.

If the folder is absent, there is nothing to do here.

